    },
    {
        "content": "<p>alexcrichton <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14533#issuecomment-5996511562\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14533\">PR #14533</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>To me this seems like an edge case where the spec is probably ambiguous about what's supposed to happen. Is this motivated by real-world usage? Or an audit? (or is the spec actually precise in this respect and I'm misremembering?)</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 629262867,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791210454
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14533#issuecomment-5997363066\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14533\">PR #14533</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>An audit, not a user report. <br>\nYou can take a look at the following code!</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/4b3cef0268cf52a079e07f1d39327121c13561a2/crates/wasi-io/wit/deps/io.wit#L184-L204\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/4b3cef0268cf52a079e07f1d39327121c13561a2/crates/wasi-io/wit/deps/io.wit#L184-L204</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/4b3cef0268cf52a079e07f1d39327121c13561a2/crates/wasi/src/p2/filesystem.rs#L288-L292\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/4b3cef0268cf52a079e07f1d39327121c13561a2/crates/wasi/src/p2/filesystem.rs#L288-L292</a></p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 629278313,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791213296
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14533#issuecomment-5997457921\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14533\">PR #14533</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The spec is clear: write requires len(contents) &lt;= n, and check-write can return ok(0). So write([]) after ok(0) is valid.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 629280191,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791213603
    },
